# CODEOWNERS: the ownership half of the selective code-owner review gate
#
# Docs: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
# The standard is musher-dev/platform ADR 0134, checked by engineering-conventions
# COMM-09 (no `*` catch-all) and COMM-10 (every anchored path exists). The other
# half is the organization ruleset's `require_code_owner_review`
# (musher-dev/infra-github#57).
#
# How review works here:
#
#   A pull request that touches NO path listed below merges on green CI alone:
#   the required checks are the gate. A pull request that touches a listed path
#   also needs its owner's approval. GitHub waives that on the owner's own pull
#   requests.
#
# What is owned, and why:
#   /.github/   the gate itself: this file
#   /.repo/     this repository's identity declaration
#   /profile/   the organization's public profile page on github.com
#
# Everything else is unowned on purpose, the default community health files and
# docs included. Listing a path is a commitment to review every change to it,
# so keep the list short.
#
# Syntax rules that bite:
#   - NEVER add a `*` catch-all (COMM-09). It makes every pull request
#     codeowned and brings back blanket review of the whole repository.
#   - LAST matching pattern wins: order from broad to specific.
#   - ALL owners for a pattern go on ONE line.
#   - Owners need EXPLICIT write access to this repo, or the entry is silently
#     ignored and the path becomes unowned. @musher-dev/engineering owns this
#     repository (musher-dev/infra-github data/managed-repositories.yaml).
#     GitHub lists ignored lines at
#     `gh api repos/musher-dev/.github/codeowners/errors`.
#   - A root-anchored path must exist (COMM-10): after a rename, the old line
#     protects nothing.

/.github/   @musher-dev/engineering
/.repo/     @musher-dev/engineering
/profile/   @musher-dev/engineering
